      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just had to do a rumenotomy on one of my heifers because of a blockage. can u give me a list of what i should be looking for in terms of recovery and signs of infection over the next week? also what should i feed her once she starts acting normal again?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Good luck with your heifer; those procedures are always a bit nerve-wracking. You'll want to watch for signs of recovery like a good, steady stream of manure, a return to normal appetite, and a decrease in any abdominal discomfort. For infection, look out for fever, excessive heat, foul-smelling discharge from the incision site, or any signs of lethargy. When she's feeling better, slowly reintroduce her usual diet, perhaps starting with easily digestible forage mixed with some palatable, high-energy feed to encourage her to eat. Remember to keep the incision clean and dry, and monitor her closely for any red flags.",
      "source": "target",
